    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1a514784-87a7-5ab6-b97c-c7e9c9572719",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=- \\frac{25}{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=- \\frac{11}{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=4.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(4)=- \\frac{11}{2}.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=- \\frac{11}{2}-(-4)=- \\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=- \\frac{3}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(- \\frac{3}{2})-(4)=- \\frac{25}{2}.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=- \\frac{25}{2}-(3)-(-4)=- \\frac{23}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=- \\frac{23}{2}$, ${x}_{2}=- \\frac{3}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=4.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{23}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
