    "question": {
      ":question/id": "11b5aeea-a381-51c8-b859-c6e1ea284a11",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y-z &=8 \\\\ y-z &=-2 \\\\ z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that $z=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(0)=-2.\n$$\n\n$$\ny=-2-(0)=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $y=-2$ and $z=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(-2)-(0)=8.\n$$\n\n$$\nx=8-(2)-(0)=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=6$, $y=-2$, and $z=0.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n⟨6,-2,0⟩.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
