      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z &=6 \\\\ y-z &=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that $z=-4.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(-4)=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{2}-(4)=- \\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $y=- \\frac{3}{2}$ and $z=-4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(- \\frac{3}{2})-(-4)=6.\n$$\n\n$$\nx=6-(- \\frac{3}{2})-(4)=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{7}{2}$, $y=- \\frac{3}{2}$, and $z=-4.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
