      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-4.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(-4)=3.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=3-(4)=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=-4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(-1)+(-4)=-3.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-3-(1)-(-4)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=0$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=-4.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n⟨0,-1,-4⟩.\n$$",
